{"pageid":1038,"title":"Abandoned Mine","displaytitle":"<span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Abandoned Mine</span>","revid":21059,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"ALTHOUGH_THE_CONTENT_ARE_MOSTLY_REMOVED._THE_LOCATION_STILL_EXISTS_TO_THIS_DAY_AND_SERVES_A_NEW_PURPOSE\">ALTHOUGH THE CONTENT ARE MOSTLY REMOVED. THE LOCATION STILL EXISTS TO THIS DAY AND SERVES A NEW PURPOSE</span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"New_Purpose_-_A_gate_to_get_back_in_time\">New Purpose - A gate to get back in time</span></h2>\n<p>Located by the right side beach of the main island map, near the way to Fairway Island on the right side, the cave still exists.\n</p><p>However, the bunker has opened.\n</p><p>A <a href=\"/wiki/Strange_Portal\" title=\"Strange Portal\">gate opened</a> with green color, teleports player into another place out of the game, when the game has only 2 islands. Return back in time.\n</p><p>The retro Oaklands\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>You will be basically back in time to the old island where landscapes are mostly flat and drivable easily back then.\n</p><p>Only the map revert is the significance change. But the map is slightly changes from that old time: Exists a portal with green whirl to teleports you back to main game. Only the sea of Finlay Island is saved, other waters are removed. The map takes the version when the <a href=\"/wiki/Lighthouse\" title=\"Lighthouse\">Lighthouse</a> are destroyed and Magma Tree no longer spawns on land (need verify on if Magma Tree still exists in that version)\n</p><p>Only you is the only player in that server, no one else joins. Progress are saved like normal.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Profits\">Profits</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Mushroom Cave aka <a href=\"/wiki/Uncertainty_Cave\" title=\"Uncertainty Cave\">Uncertainty Cave</a> will gets easier to reach since there are literal maps point exactly to its location</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Mysterious_Mushrooms\" title=\"Mysterious Mushrooms\">Mysterious Mushroom</a> are easier (?) to get since the cave back then has short roof, making the mushrooms closer to ground</li>\n<li>Since the sea are not 100% filled like back then (only the main island has proper water), you can easily gather <a href=\"/wiki/Kelp\" title=\"Kelp\">Kelp</a> just like a normal tree on the ground at second island</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Classic_Store\" title=\"Classic Store\">The classic shop</a> are easier to reach back then (at the back of main island), allowing you to buy classic items easily</li>\n<li><b>Quests are not tested, need more people performs it in this specific version.</b></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Disadvantages\">Disadvantages</span></h3>\n<ul><li>Base that has basement will be half-flooded, making difficulties into basement.</li>\n<li>Minimaps are not loaded, making players has to use self-intuition to figure the paths (except old players who didn't have maps back then but still remember the way)</li>\n<li>Selling still works but by individual patches (if using <a href=\"/wiki/The_Oak_Depot\" title=\"The Oak Depot\">Oak Depot</a>'s selling pit or <a href=\"/wiki/Radical_Shack\" title=\"Radical Shack\">Radical Shack</a>'s selling pit), because there was no united <a href=\"/wiki/Resource_Hub\" title=\"Resource Hub\">Resource Hub</a> back then.</li>\n<li>Shops are also return to old times, meaning some items are not available to buy</li></ul>\n<table class=\"notice\" style=\"border-radius:15px; border: 3px solid #690B0B; background:#8C0F0F; font-size:90%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><p style=\"margin-bottom: .3em;\"><span style=\"font-size: 125%; font-weight: semi-bold;\">Removed</span><br />\n<span><i>The following content has been removed from the game or does not exist.</i></span></p>\n<div></div>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><as